    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** providing the clear anchor for the lineup; his 82.97 efficiency score is fueled by a favorable 4.59 xERA matchup against Mikolas and a significant platoon boost, making him our primary candidate for multi-hit output. Joining him in the top tier are **Kyle Schwarber** (70.49) and **Trea Turner** (69.83). Both benefit from the favorable matchup against Cameron, with **Trea Turner** providing the essential speed floor we prioritize in this 5x5 format. While **Christian Yelich** faces a tougher test against May, his dynamic platoon advantage (13% boost) keeps his projection firmly in the strong category (64.83), ensuring we maximize our potential in the R and RBI categories.\n\nStrategic platoon edges and environmental factors heavily influenced the lower-tier decisions. **Casey Schmitt** (55.03) remains a start despite a middling 3.71 xERA opponent, as his 11% dynamic platoon boost and the high stolen base potential offered by the pitcher\u2019s delivery cadence align with our scarcity-based strategy. Conversely, **Junior Caminero** (49.84) and **Kazuma Okamoto** (52.91) are hovering near the marginal threshold due to tougher pitching assignments; **Junior Caminero** in particular takes a hit from an elite 2.98 xERA opponent. **Carson Benge** (60.60) secured the final starting outfield spot, though his status warrants monitoring due to a 34% rain risk in his contest against L\u00f3pez. With **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, **Caleb Durbin**, **Colt Keith**, and **Hyeseong Kim** all currently unavailable due to off-days or minor league assignments, our depth is constrained, leaving us with a straightforward rotation of the active roster. We will keep a close watch on **Carson Benge**\u2019s status as first pitch approaches to determine if an emergency pivot is required.",
